  "title": "Security hardening: tombstone revocation for API keys and service principals",
  "description": "",
  "acceptance": {
    "criteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC-1",
        "text": "API-key and service-principal revocation keep a tombstone (revokedAt, revokedReason); the presented revoked credential is reported REVOKED, a wrong secret stays UNKNOWN",
        "met": true,
        "evidenceRef": "PR #289 / docs/n8n-lego/evidence/P5-M01-EVIDENCE.md; main 27191091 fresh verification"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-2",
        "text": "Revoking an unknown or already revoked id is a silent no-op without a second audit event; upstream response shape unchanged",
        "met": true,
        "evidenceRef": "PR #289 / docs/n8n-lego/evidence/P5-M01-EVIDENCE.md; main 27191091 fresh verification"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-3",
        "text": "Tombstones are bounded per owner and kind (oldest pruned, live never pruned); lists and the live-key limit ignore tombstones",
        "met": true,
        "evidenceRef": "PR #289 / docs/n8n-lego/evidence/P5-M01-EVIDENCE.md; main 27191091 fresh verification"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-4",
